<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Razès</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Razès is a historical region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/languedoc">Languedoc</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, in the upper Aude valley around Limoux, named after the old town of Rhedae. A Carolingian county, it was joined to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carcassonne">Carcassonne</a> and passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-trencavel">Trencavel</a> viscounts in the 11th century, and after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albigensian-crusade">Albigensian Crusade</a> it came under the French crown.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/razes.jpg" alt="Razès" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: fr:Utilisateur:Paternel 1 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Le_Raz%C3%A8s_vue_de_Rennes-le-Ch%C3%A2teau.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
